---
import Pagina from "../../layouts/Pagina.astro";
import ListaFrases from "../../components/ListaFrases.astro";
import { SITIO, RUTAS } from "../../lib/obra.js";

const r = RUTAS.en;
const frases = [
  "Just because. Which is the best reason.",
  "It's not your birthday. That's why.",
  "I saw this and thought of you. End of explanation.",
  "You don't need a date to remember someone.",
  "For no reason, which is how you really care.",
  "I'm not celebrating anything. I'm celebrating you.",
  "An ordinary Tuesday deserves a gift too.",
  "You owe me nothing. Not even a thank you.",
  "This isn't for something. It's for someone.",
  "I felt like it. You can't argue with that.",
  "So today has something different in it.",
  "Don't open it looking for the why. There isn't one.",
  "Some gifts announce themselves. This one doesn't.",
  "Because the calendar doesn't decide when I think of you.",
  "A small thing for a normal day.",
  "I saw it, it was you, I brought it.",
  "It's not an apology or a celebration. It's a gift.",
  "Giving for no reason is the strangest way of saying yes."
];
const ld = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Words for a gift given for no reason", inLanguage: "en",
  author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Solzimer" }, datePublished: "2026-11-11",
  mainEntityOfPage: SITIO + r.frases, image: SITIO + "/og.png"
};
---
<Pagina
  lang="en"
  titulo="Just-because gift quotes: words for a gift given for no reason"
  descripcion="18 short lines to go with a just-because gift: no birthday, no anniversary, no excuse. Original and free to use, for a card or a message."
  ruta={r.frases}
  alternativas={[{ lang: "es", href: RUTAS.es.frases }, { lang: "pt", href: RUTAS.pt.frases }]}
  ld={ld}
>
  <h1>Words for a gift given <em>for no reason</em></h1>
  <p class="entrada">For when there is no birthday, no anniversary, no excuse. You just felt like it.</p>
  <p>A just-because gift is slightly awkward: the person receiving it looks for the why. The line that goes with it does not have to explain. It has to make clear there is nothing to explain.</p>

  <ListaFrases frases={frases} copiar="copy" copiado="copied ✓" />

  <p class="dato">These lines were written for this page. They are free to use: copy them, change them, sign them with your name.</p>

  <h2>How to use them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>On a card.</strong> One line, by hand. The less it explains, the better.</li>
    <li><strong>In a message.</strong> Send it before the gift, with no other context. The mystery is part of it.</li>
    <li><strong>Forever.</strong> In <a href={r.cielo}><em>Sin motivo</em></a>, an artwork, you can <a href={r.estrella}>gift a star</a> and leave the line written as its dedication, permanently.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why give for no reason</h2>
  <p>A birthday gift answers to a date. A gift for no reason answers to nothing, and that is why it says more: that someone thought of you on a day when they did not have to.</p>
  <p>That idea is where <a href={r.sobre}><em>Sin motivo</em></a> comes from, a work that asks one question: does anyone give something just because?</p>
  <p class="accion"><a href={r.cielo}>see the sky →</a></p>
</Pagina>
